# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform, not just the ones
# that default to it.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout applies `core.autocrlf=true` — which is the
# default on the GitHub Actions Windows runner, the only runner this project
# has — and every text file arrives with CRLF. Biome's formatter emits LF, so
# `biome ci .` then reports "File content differs from formatting output" for
# every file in the repository, including ones no commit has ever touched. The
# failure looks like a formatting bug and is not one.
#
# Fixing it here rather than by setting Biome's `lineEnding` is deliberate: the
# same transform reaches `rustfmt`, YAML, the shell in `ci.yml`'s `run:` blocks
# and `scripts/*.mjs`. One rule covers all of them, and `.gitattributes`
# overrides `core.autocrlf`, so it holds whatever a contributor has configured.
#
# Everything committed here is already LF, so this changes no stored blob —
# only what lands in a working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. `text=auto` detects these anyway; naming them means a corrupt icon
# can never be one heuristic away.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.mp4  binary
